```text
FINANCE COMMITTEE
MINUTES
Due to the Martin Luther King Jr. holiday, a meeting of the Finance Committee was instead held
on Tuesday, January 16, 2024, in Committee Room 104 and via electronic meeting, starting at
12:00 p.m. Those in attendance were as follows:
COMMITTEE MEMBERS: Dr. Michelle Aldrich, Chairwoman, Richard Johnson (via Zoom),
and Jeff White. Absent: Bryan Cook
AGENDA ITEMS
26.
LEASES/CONTRACTS/LEGAL:
a)
Human Services Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and United Way of
Laramie
County
to
provide
funding
to
community
agencies
and
monitor
performance of community programs. (20 19-2022 Optional 1% Sales Tax Fund)
Mr. White moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $197,524.00 for the period of 2 years,
seconded by Mr. Johnson. Motion carried with Mr. White voting “YES” and Mr. Johnson voting
“NO” and Chairwoman Aldrich voting “YES”, breaking the tie.
Vicki Nemecek, Public Works Director, provided a staff report.
b)
Cooperative Agreement between the City of Cheyenne, Laramie County, and
United Way of Laramie County to create a Human Services Advisory Council and
to coordinate and refine human services funding and delivery systems. (2023-2026
Optional 1% Sales Tax Fund)
Mr. White moved to approve in an amount not to exceed $42,000.00 for the period of 4 years,
seconded by Mr. Johnson. Motion carried with Mr. White voting “YES” and Mr. Johnson voting
“NO” and Chainvoman Aldrich voting “YES”, breaking the tie.
Vicki Nemecek, Public Works Director, provided a staff report and committee member White
commented on the item.
c)
Purchase and Sale Agreement between the City of Cheyenne and Sunflower Ridge
LC3 for the purchase of the BEAST Foundation Facility located at 2900 Sunflower
Road, Cheyenne, Wyoming. (General Fund Reserves)
Mr. White moved to approve a purchase amount not to exceed $4,250,000.00, and a donation to
the City in the amount of $750,000.00, seconded by Mr. Johnson. Motion carried by unanimous
voice vote.
```

